  'limpopo-police-election-security-voting-hours-2026-10-30',
  'Limpopo police rate five voting stations medium risk ahead of 4 November vote',
  'Community', '2026-10-30', 'Review Online', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/review-online/news-headlines/local-news/2026/10/30/police-iec-outline-election-security-plans-for-limpopo/',
  'Police say five Limpopo voting stations are rated medium risk and none high risk, with voting in Polokwane running from 07:00 to 21:00 on 4 November.',
  'Limpopo police have told the province they are ready for the local government elections on 4 November. At a readiness briefing in Polokwane, the provincial police commissioner, Lt Gen Jan Scheepers, said five voting stations in the province have been rated medium risk and that none are rated high risk.

Police say the security work is driven by intelligence assessments and coordinated by ProvJoints, the provincial joint operational and intelligence body. The plan includes highly visible policing, intelligence gathering, targeted operations and investigations into electoral offences. The SANDF and the State Security Agency are supporting the operation. Provincial traffic officers will help escort ballot papers and other election materials. Police say they will act against intimidation, violence, vandalism and unauthorised dangerous weapons inside the perimeter of voting stations.

For voters, the Electoral Commission says polling in Polokwane starts at 07:00 and ends at 21:00 on 4 November, and people still waiting in line at 21:00 can cast their ballots. Special votes take place on 2 and 3 November. The IEC reports that Polokwane has 37 political parties contesting 45 wards, and that Limpopo has more than 3 million registered voters. The Department of Home Affairs is extending the hours of its offices and mobile offices so voters can collect ID documents or replace lost ones.

Police have asked parties, candidates and supporters to follow the Electoral Code of Conduct and respect differing views. They have also warned residents against sharing fake news or unverified information on social media that could cause panic or incite violence.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/review-online/news-headlines/local-news/2026/10/30/police-iec-outline-election-security-plans-for-limpopo/", "https://www.timeslive.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-10-29-limpopo-police-identify-five-medium-risk-voting-stations-ahead-of-elections/"]',
  'agent'
);
